
Add a cluster to Argocd
========================

1) get the Kubernetes context name 

  kubectl config get-contexts -o name
2) login to Argocd via cli

 argocd login <server_url:port)

 argocd login 16.59.39.4:30506 --insecure
username: admin
password: your password


get the kubeconfig file of the cluster want to add. 
export it and get the context name 

3 Export the kubeconfig file in that active powershell. 
$env:KUBECONFIG = "$(Get-Location)/../a single cluster.yaml"

or Git bash
-----------
export KUBECONFIG=../mysinglecluster.yaml 
 kubectl config get-contexts -o namey
